      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Closing at OP's request. \nExplanation:\n> It seems that some pack I had overwrote one of Unity's default shaders, and despite deleting that pack things were still broken. My understanding is that if the shader is imported as an actual separate shader things would work fine, but since it was directly conflicting with one of Unity's built-in shaders then everything went to crap, even with it having been deleted.",
